# Authentication Patterns

This project uses a centralized auth system in `js/auth.js`. All pages in protected folders (`crm/`, `connect/`, `team/`, `kba/`, etc.) must follow these patterns to avoid false relogins caused by Firebase token refresh cycles.

## Core Concept

Firebase briefly sets `auth.currentUser = null` during every token refresh (~every 1 hour). `auth.js` has a 12-hour protection window that keeps `currentAuthState.isLoggedIn = true` during these moments. Any page code that checks `auth.currentUser` directly — without consulting auth.js — will falsely kick users out.

---

## Rule 1: Always guard redirects with `isTrulyLoggedOut()`

When a page has its own `onAuthStateChanged` listener, NEVER redirect or show a session-expired banner without checking `window.isTrulyLoggedOut()` first.

```js
// ❌ BAD — redirects during normal token refresh cycles
onAuthStateChanged(auth, (user) => {
  if (!user) {
    window.location.href = '../login.html';
  }
});

// ✅ GOOD — respects auth.js protection window
onAuthStateChanged(auth, (user) => {
  if (!user) {
    if (window.isTrulyLoggedOut?.()) {
      window.location.href = '../login.html';
    } else {
      console.log('🛡️ Suppressing false logout — auth.js protection active');
    }
  }
});
```

The same applies to any session-expired banner or alert — wrap it with `if (window.isTrulyLoggedOut?.())`.

---

## Rule 2: Never check `auth.currentUser` directly for session UI

`auth.currentUser` can be null during token refresh even when the user is legitimately logged in. Always use `window.getCurrentAuthState()` or `window.isTrulyLoggedOut()` instead.

```js
// ❌ BAD
if (!auth.currentUser) {
  showSessionExpiredBanner();
  return;
}

// ✅ GOOD
if (window.isTrulyLoggedOut?.()) {
  showSessionExpiredBanner();
  return;
}
```

---

## Rule 3: Do NOT implement your own token refresh interval

`auth.js` already runs a centralized token refresh every 45 minutes with cross-tab coordination. Adding a second interval on the same page creates duplicate simultaneous refreshes that generate noisy localStorage events, which can trigger false logout detection.

If a page truly needs its own backup refresh, follow this template exactly:

```js
// ✅ ONLY if a page-level backup refresh is absolutely necessary
const MAX_TOKEN_REFRESH_FAILURES = 10; // Must be 10 — never lower
let tokenRefreshFailureCount = 0;

async function refreshAuthToken() {
  try {
    if (auth.currentUser) {
      // Defer to auth.js centralized refresh if available
      if (window.refreshAuthToken && window.refreshAuthToken !== refreshAuthToken) {
        await window.refreshAuthToken();
      } else {
        await auth.currentUser.getIdToken(true);
      }
      tokenRefreshFailureCount = 0;
    }
  } catch (error) {
    tokenRefreshFailureCount++;
    if (tokenRefreshFailureCount >= MAX_TOKEN_REFRESH_FAILURES) {
      console.error('Token refresh failed — auth.js will handle session state');
      tokenRefreshFailureCount = 0; // Reset; keep trying
      // DO NOT alert() or redirect here — auth.js handles genuine expiry
    }
  }
}

// Must use 45 minutes to align with auth.js — never use 20 minutes or lower
setInterval(refreshAuthToken, 45 * 60 * 1000);
```

---

## Rule 4: Let `auth.js` and `folder-protection.js` do their jobs

- Do not call `setPersistence()` on pages that load `auth.js` — it already sets `browserLocalPersistence`
- Do not re-initialize Firebase if `auth.js` is loaded — use `window.auth`, `window.db`, `window.firebaseReady`
- Do not add a second `protectFolder()` call — `folder-protection.js` auto-runs via `autoProtectFromPath()`

```js
// ✅ Correct way to get auth in a page that loads auth.js
await window.firebaseReady;
const auth = window.auth;
const db = window.db;
```

---

## Useful globals provided by `auth.js`

| Global | What it does |
|---|---|
| `window.isTrulyLoggedOut()` | Returns `true` only when user is genuinely logged out (not mid-refresh) |
| `window.getCurrentAuthState()` | Returns current auth state object: `{ isLoggedIn, isVerified, user, isChecking }` |
| `window.firebaseReady` | Promise that resolves when Firebase + auth are fully initialized |
| `window.requireAuthResilient(msg, ms)` | Async auth check with retry; redirects only after timeout |
| `window.refreshAuthToken()` | Centralized token refresh — use this instead of `getIdToken(true)` directly |
